# Who has to have read a change before it lands, for the files where a change is a
# change to what gets shipped rather than to what the app does.
#
# A pull request that edits a workflow can print a secret, send an artefact
# somewhere else, or sign something with the key - and it looks like every other
# green pull request while doing it. Same for the packaging: those files decide what
# bytes a package manager hands somebody who types `brew install nib`, and for the
# Tauri configuration, which is where the capabilities, the updater's public key and
# the bundle's identity live. Dependabot opens pull requests against the first of
# these every week (see dependabot.yml), which is exactly why they are listed: a
# routine bump to an action is the change nobody looks twice at.
#
# Nothing else has an owner. The app is reviewed by whoever is reviewing.

# The release machinery, and everything it is handed.
/.github/ @lxorb
/.github/workflows/** @lxorb

# What a package manager ships, and the digests that say it is the release's own
# bytes; see packaging/linux.md and apps/desktop/test/packaging.test.ts.
/packaging/** @lxorb

# The capabilities the webviews get, the updater's public key, the signing and
# bundling of the app itself.
/apps/desktop/src-tauri/tauri.conf.json @lxorb
/apps/desktop/src-tauri/capabilities/** @lxorb
/apps/desktop/src-tauri/gen/android/app/build.gradle.kts @lxorb

# The dependency graph the release is built out of, by hash.
/pnpm-lock.yaml @lxorb
/apps/desktop/src-tauri/Cargo.lock @lxorb
